Patch G3, parry3d (rung 2, task T0b): the allow-list entries parry3d-f64
0.31.1 needs as a test-only dependency of eng-collision-grid. Apply it
only if the owner's answer to O4 picks parry3d-f64 for the collision
oracle instead of brute force; T5 then builds both oracles. It applies
after any of the three G3 variants (g3-crate-batch-3.patch,
g3-crate-batch-3-shim-module.patch, g3-crate-batch-3-no-shim.patch):
its one hunk's context is the end of the batch 3 list, the same in all
three.

What: `[bans] allow` gains 18 names in a block after batch 3, under a
comment of their own. They were resolved against the real lock (main with
both G2 patches, batch 3 as in g3-crate-batch-3.patch, and
`parry3d-f64 = "=0.31.1"` in eng-collision-grid's `[dev-dependencies]`, in
a scratch copy only). Cargo.lock gained 19 packages. The 19th,
downcast-rs 2.0.2, is allowed already by name (batch 2 has its 1.x), so it
needs no entry. The plan's 39-crate tree was counted from nothing; the
rest of it is in the allow-list already.

